# wp-secmon: account used to check a site, when it is not the owner of the
# WordPress directory.
#
#   <wordpress root>   <account>
#
# Use "-" as the account to never check a site. The account can never be root.
# Typical LEMP case: code owned by root, PHP-FPM pool running as www-data.
#
# /var/www/example.com/public     www-data
# /var/www/staging.example.com    -
